_ORDER) | MUST: error contract requirement |\n| ShipmentRepository.kt | Added `findByOrderId()` method | MUST: query shipments by order to check for CONFIRMED |\n| OrderController.kt | Injected ShipmentRepository, added cancel() endpoint at POST /{orderId}/cancel | MUST: endpoint implementation |\n| ShipmentController.kt | Injected OrderRepository, added cancelled order validation in create() | MUST: prevent shipment creation on cancelled orders |\n| OrderControllerTest.kt | Added 9 new test methods (13 total, was 4) | MUST: cover all cancel scenarios |\n\n**Unresolved findings:** None. All requirements are implemented and tested.\n\n```\n<<PHASE:DONE>>\n```\n\nRequirement   Add POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel endpoint with order status tracking, cascading shipment cancellation, idempotent retry handling, and conflict prevention for confirmed shipments.\n\nChanged       \n  Order.kt — added status field with OrderStatus enum (ACTIVE/CANCELLED)\n  ApiError.kt — added error codes for cancel and create-shipment validation\n  ShipmentRepository.kt — added findByOrderId() to query shipments for cancellation cascade\n  OrderController.kt — added cancel endpoint with all business logic (CONFIRMED check, idempotency, cascade)\n  ShipmentController.kt — added cancelled order validation to prevent shipment creation\n  OrderControllerTest.kt — added 9 tests covering cancel, cascade, idempotency, conflicts, 404, and create-on-cancelled\n\nTests         \n  cancel an active order returns CANCELLED status — verifies cancel changes status\n  cancel an active order persists the cancellation — verifies write to repository\n  cancel an already cancelled order succeeds idempotently — verifies repeated calls succeed\n  cancel returns 404 for non-existent order — verifies 404 with error envelope\n  cancel cascades to CREATED shipments — verifies both CREATED shipments become CANCELLED\n  cancel fails with 409 if any shipment is CONFIRMED — verifies 409, no state change\n  cannot create shipment for cancelled order — verifies shipment creation blocked with 409\n  can create shipment for non-existent order — verifies current behavior preserved\n  creates an order with ACTIVE status — verifies default status\n\nVerification  Command: `./mvnw clean test` from sample-service/\n              Result: BUILD SUCCESS, Tests run: 22, Failures: 0, Errors: 0\n              All existing tests pass, all new tests pass.\n\nNot done      Nothing — all acceptance criteria satisfied, all tests pass, build succeeds, no forbidden files modified."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":604,"cache_read_input_tokens":39174,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":604},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5db10471-faf5-4d2d-9ad3-060f8029a4f8","uuid":"9d14bf91-4d81-4ed0-9833-3c44e5efd7e1","timestamp":"2026-09-26T19:02:09.691Z","request_id":"req_011CfSZusMndXbsGbP1QzuJE"}
